-- ----- fragment: minion_isaiah_34.sql (Isaiah 34) -----
-- Chapter: Isaiah 34 — THE DAY OF VENGEANCE / the judgment of the nations, focused on Edom. The
-- dark twin of ch 35 and the lateral mate of the ch63 Bozrah winepress (already built — referenced,
-- NOT duplicated). The covenant-lawsuit opens with a summons of all nations: *Come near, ye nations,
-- to hear... For the indignation of Yahuah (LORD) is upon all nations... he hath delivered them to
-- the slaughter* (34:1-2). The host of heaven is dissolved and *the heavens shall be rolled together
-- as a scroll* (34:4 = the sixth seal). The sword of Yahuah comes down upon Idumea/Edom and finds a
-- *sacrifice in Bozrah, and a great slaughter in the land of Idumea* (34:5-6) — *for it is the day of
-- the LORD'S vengeance, and the year of recompences for the controversy of Zion* (34:8). The land
-- becomes *burning pitch... the smoke thereof shall go up for ever* (34:9-10); the unclean
-- birds/beasts possess it (34:11-15); and the chapter closes with the sure word: *Seek ye out of the
-- book of Yahuah (LORD), and read: no one of these shall fail* (34:16). FRAMED as covenant-lawsuit /
-- the day of recompence — Edom is the archetype of the SYSTEM of nations that exalted itself against
-- Zion; it is that system that is judged. Victims, not enemies; the controversy of Zion is righteous.
-- Tag: isa34   Temp view: _s303_isa34_lookup
-- Sort band: base 26825, step 3 -> threads at 26825, 26828, 26831, 26834, 26837, 26840 (6 threads)
-- Source of EVERY row: 'canon','isaiah',34,v
--
-- Isaiah 34 coverage:
--   ★★ v.1-2 (Come near, ye nations... the indignation of Yahuah (LORD) is upon all nations... he
--          hath delivered them to the slaughter)
--        NT:     ★★ Revelation 14:19 (gathered the vine of the earth, and cast it into the great
--                winepress of the wrath of Elohim (God)), 14:20 (the winepress was trodden... blood
--                came out), ★ Revelation 19:15 (he treadeth the winepress of the fierceness and wrath
--                of El Shaddai) — THREAD 1 (the great winepress; the slaughter of the nations)
--        Extras: none warranted (the winepress weave is carried canon-to-canon; Bozrah handled in T3)
--        Tanakh: ★ Joel 3:14 (Multitudes, multitudes in the valley of decision), 3:12 (there will I
--                sit to judge all the heathen) — THREAD 1 lateral (the valley of decision)
--   ★ v.4 (the host of heaven shall be dissolved, and the heavens shall be rolled together as a
--          scroll... as the leaf falleth off from the vine, and as a falling fig from the fig tree)
--        NT:     ★ Revelation 6:13-14 (the stars of heaven fell... as a fig tree casteth her untimely
--                figs... the heaven departed as a scroll when it is rolled together), ★ Matthew 24:29
--                (the stars shall fall from heaven, and the powers of the heavens shall be shaken) —
--                THREAD 2 (the sixth seal). NOTE existing reverse thread anchored in Rev 6 laterals
--                here (Joel 2 / Isa 34); this is the Isaiah-34-SOURCED forward weave, distinct anchor.
--        Extras: none warranted distinct
--        Tanakh: ★ Joel 3:15 (the sun and the moon shall be darkened, and the stars shall withdraw
--                their shining) — THREAD 2 lateral
--   ★ v.5-6,8 (my sword shall be bathed in heaven... upon Idumea... Yahuah (LORD) hath a sacrifice in
--          Bozrah, and a great slaughter in the land of Idumea... the day of the LORD'S vengeance, and
--          the year of recompences for the controversy of Zion)
--        NT:     ★ Revelation 19:17 (gather yourselves together unto the supper of the great Elohim),
--                19:18 (That ye may eat the flesh of kings... and the flesh of all men) — THREAD 3 (the
--                fowls' supper; the sacrifice of the nations)
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★★ Isaiah 63:1 (Who is this that cometh from Edom, with dyed garments from Bozrah)
--                + 63:4 (the day of vengeance is in mine heart, and the year of my redeemed is come) —
--                THREAD 3 lateral (the ch63 Bozrah winepress, SAME day-of-vengeance/year pair;
--                referenced not duplicated); ★ Obadiah 1:15 (the day of Yahuah (LORD) is near upon all
--                the heathen... thy reward shall return upon thine own head) — THREAD 3 (Edom archetype)
--   ★ v.9-10 (the land thereof shall become burning pitch... the smoke thereof shall go up for ever)
--        NT:     ★ Revelation 14:11 (the smoke of their torment ascendeth up for ever and ever), ★
--                Revelation 18:18 (when they saw the smoke of her burning), ★ Revelation 19:3 (her
--                smoke rose up for ever and ever) — THREAD 4 (the smoke that rises for ever)
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: woven in prose (Sodom-Gomorrah brimstone backdrop); no separate add forced
--   ★ v.11-15 (the cormorant and the bittern shall possess it... an habitation of dragons, and a court
--          for owls... the screech owl... the great owl make her nest)
--        NT:     ★ Revelation 18:2 (Babylon... is become the habitation of devils, and the hold of
--                every foul spirit, and a cage of every unclean and hateful bird) — THREAD 5 (the
--                desolation possessed by unclean creatures)
--        Extras: none warranted (clean witness preferred)
--        Tanakh: woven in prose (the line of confusion / stones of emptiness = Gen 1:2 tohu/bohu echo);
--                no separate add forced
--   ★ v.16-17 (Seek ye out of the book of Yahuah (LORD), and read: no one of these shall fail... for
--          my mouth it hath commanded, and his spirit it hath gathered them)
--        NT:     ★ Matthew 24:35 (Heaven and earth shall pass away, but my words shall not pass away)
